MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

quickstart sequences bootstrap then roadmap on one real, current
decision in the same sitting, so a first-time user feels this system's
value before deciding whether to keep using it, instead of being left
to chain skills together on their own.

plugins/kms/hooks/hooks.json ships a Claude Code SessionStart hook
(plugins/kms/hooks/steward-nudge.sh) that surfaces a note to the agent
when HEAD's commit is under 4 hours old, suggesting it mention running
steward to the user. This auto-activates for anyone who installs the
plugin, with zero manual settings.json setup — the closest this plugin
gets to ambient, not purely opt-in, knowledge capture. The mechanism
went through two corrections during this session, both caught before
being left as silent bugs: the original SessionEnd version was a
complete no-op (that event's output is discarded entirely, confirmed
via primary docs), and after switching to SessionStart, a /code-review
pass caught two shell bugs (an exit-code-only work-tree check, and an
unguarded negative age on clock skew) plus flagged the inline
one-line JSON shell command as unreadable/untestable. All three are
fixed, and the corrected script was verified empirically against a
recent commit, an old commit, a bare repo, and a future-dated commit.

README/GitHub metadata were also brought up to date: static license and
"Claude Code Plugin" badges (no CI exists to back anything more), plus
previously empty/stale GitHub topics and description synced via `gh
repo edit` to reflect the plugin's actual current scope.

